# Hospital Data Analysis using SQL

## 📌 Project Overview

This project is a practical SQL data analysis project completed as part of the **30 Days SQL Micro Course**.

The project uses hospital data stored in an Excel dataset and analyzes it using **PostgreSQL and pgAdmin**.

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies

- PostgreSQL
- pgAdmin 4
- SQL
- Excel

## 🔍 Analysis Performed

1. Total Number of Patients
2. Average Number of Doctors per Hospital
3. Top 3 Departments with the Highest Number of Patients
4. Hospital with the Maximum Medical Expenses
5. Daily Average Medical Expenses
6. Longest Hospital Stay
7. Total Patients Treated Per City
8. Average Length of Stay Per Department
9. Department with the Lowest Number of Patients
10. Monthly Medical Expenses Report

## 💡 SQL Concepts Used

- SELECT
- SUM()
- AVG()
- GROUP BY
- ORDER BY
- LIMIT
- DATEDIFF
- Date Functions
- Aggregate Functions

## 📂 Project Files

- `Hospital_Data.xlsx` — Hospital dataset
- `Hospital_Data_SQL_Analysis.sql` — SQL queries used for analysis
- `30_Days_SQL_Hospital_Assignment.pdf` — Completed assignment

## 🎯 Learning Outcome

This project helped me strengthen my practical SQL skills and understand how SQL can be used to analyze real-world hospital data and generate useful insights.

